// A pedal mark sits on its OWN staff's below-baseline. It must NOT be pushed past a
// lyric line elsewhere in the system: the piano's "Ped." / "*" stay under the piano
// staff, not dropped below the vocal lyrics. The system-wide lyric floor is for jump
// marks (D.C./D.S./Fine) only; it used to catch pedals too. Regression lock.
title "A pedal keeps its own staff baseline, clear of the vocal lyrics"
time 4/4
key c major
part voc { clef treble }
part pno { clef bass }
section A {
  voc { c'4 d' e' f' | }
  lyrics words sings voc { la la la la | }
  pno { c4 d@sustainOn e f@sustainOff | }
}
form main { A }
score main "pedal-below-lyrics" { staff voc  lyrics words  staff pno }
